===Etymology===
From {{inh|id|ms|suku}}, ultimately from {{inh|id|poz-pro|*suku|t=one quarter; designation for a division of society, probably a lineage}}.<ref>{{cite-journal|en|author=Robert Blust|title=The Challenge of Semantic Reconstruction: Proto-Malayo-Polynesian *suku 'lineage; quarter'?|work=Oceanic Linguistics|page=247–256|year=2017|url=https://muse.jhu.edu/article/661347|volume=56|issue=1|issn=1527-9421|doi=10.1353/ol.2017.0010}}</ref>
* The sense {{m-g|clan}} is a {{semantic loan|id|min|suku|nocap=1}}.
* The sense {{m-g|footer}} is a {{sl|id|en|footer|nocap=1}}.
* Displaced {{sl|id|nl|term|t=term|notext=1}} by Komisi Bahasa Indonesia as published on Kanpō/[[berita pemerintah|Berita Pemerintah]] No.38 Year III Month 3 (2604) in 1944.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|id|[ˈsuku]}}
* {{hyphenation|id|su|ku}}

